  "term": "Steele–Richardson–Olszewski syndrome",
  "definition": "Steele–Richardson–Olszewski syndrome is a degenerative central nervous system disorder, also known as progressive supranuclear palsy. It typically begins in midlife and slowly worsens over several years, causing problems with balance, eye movement control, speech, swallowing, and posture.",
